## What is here

`.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/` is a copy of JFast Suite: plain HTML,
CSS and JavaScript, no build. Every page is a finished screen in the Nexora look, and together they are the
catalogue of patterns the design supports.

| Page | Shows |
| --- | --- |
| `.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/index.html` | The landing: hero, feature grid, the liquid ribbon, reveal cards, pricing |
| `.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/crm.html` | An ERP/CRM console: KPI cards, client directory, sales pipeline, team chat |
| `.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/pagos.html` | A payment gateway: card form, payment methods, invoicing |
| `.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/social.html` | A company social feed: posts, composer, profile cards |
| `.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/tablas.html` | Operations tables: dense data, filters, row actions, status badges |
| `.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/widgets.html` | Controls: selects, action sheets, modals, the colour-customisation drawer |

Open it in a browser -- relative paths, so it needs a local server, not
`file://`:

```bash
cd .jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite && python -m http.server 4600
# http://localhost:4600/crm.html
```

An agent without a browser reads the page's markup and the `<style>` block at
its top: most of each page's look is there, not in the shared stylesheet.

## It is a reference, never a dependency

- **Do not link these files from the app**, import them, or copy the folder
  into `src/` or the public folder. The app has its own
  `src/nexora/nexora.css`, and two stylesheets describing one look drift
  apart.
- **The images are demo art** (cars, backdrops), shrunk to keep this copy
  small. Do not ship them in the product.
- **The suite loads three.js r128 from a CDN.** The app already has the ribbon
  -- `src/nexora/liquid.js`, three.js from npm in its own lazy chunk, with the
  3D / 2D / off switch. Do not add a second one.

## Bringing a pattern across

1. **Look for it in the project first.** The app ships `CardBox`, `BaseButton`,
   `BaseBadge`, `BaseInput`, `BaseModal`, `EmptyState`, `SkeletonLoader`,
   `SectionTitleLineWithButton` and `ToastHost` in `src/components/`, and
   `src/nexora/nexora.css` already has `card-panel`, `btn-modern`,
   `badge-status`, the `nx-*` shell and the KPI cards. A suite widget that is
   one of those with different content is that component, not a new one.
2. **Otherwise, move the CSS into the project's stylesheet.** Take the rules
   from the page's `<style>` block, or from
   `.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/assets/css/nexora.css`, into
   `src/nexora/nexora.css`, inside the same components layer. Rename them
   `nx-<thing>` so they cannot collide with Tailwind or with another page.
3. **Translate the tokens.** Most custom properties exist in both with the same
   name (`--c-accent`, `--card-bg`, `--text-main`, ...). The suite-only ones map
   like this:

   | Suite | Use in the project |
   | --- | --- |
   | `--primary`, `--accent`, `--primary-rgb` | `rgb(var(--c-accent))`, `var(--c-accent)` |
   | `--primary-glow`, `--liquid-glow`, `--shadow-glow` | `rgb(var(--c-glow) / <alpha>)` |
   | `--primary-hover`, `--primary-light` | `color-mix()` over `--c-accent`, as `style.css` does for `brand-*` |
   | `--text-muted` | `var(--text-dim)` |
   | `--border-color` | `var(--card-border)` |
   | `--shadow-*` | `var(--float-shadow)`, or the card's own shadow |

   Never write the suite's hex colours in: the accent is the viewer's choice
   (the picker in the top bar), and a hard-coded ruby ignores it.
4. **Make it a component** in `src/components/`, named like the others, with
   props for what changes between uses. Pages -- `src/Modulo<Name>/Pages/` --
   use the component; they do not carry the markup.
5. **Check it in both themes and at 375 px.** The suite is dark-first; the
   project is not. In `nexora.css` light is the plain `:root`, and dark is
   defined twice -- under `prefers-color-scheme: dark` and under
   `:root[data-theme="dark"]`. Use the tokens and both come for free; a colour
   you had to write by hand needs a value in all three places.

## Interactions

The suite's behaviour is in
`.jfast/skills/nexora-reference/suite/assets/js/nexora-common.js` -- menus,
sheets, modals, the customisation drawer, count-ups -- as DOM code. Read it for *what*
happens; write it again as component state in the app's framework. Do not
bring `document.querySelector` wiring into a Vue or React page.
